WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.836
-Our guest tonight is an
Emmy-winning actor you know from

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.171
shows such as "The Office," "The
Practice," and "Boston Legal."

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.006
He stars in the ninth season
of "The Blacklist,"

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:09.375
which returns to NBC on
Thursday, October 21st.

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:10.577
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.245
-During the past two years,

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:17.283
I've learned what to hold on to
and what to let go of.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:23.823
If I look at that, if I come
back even once...

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:27.093
I fear all that work
will be for nothing.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.895
There would be names
to be taken,

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.764
people would be held
accountable.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:34.634
Down the line,
things would get very dark.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:38.004
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend James Spader.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.807
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:48.247 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:50.283
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:56.355 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.355 --> 00:01:02.395 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.131
James, welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:08.000
Fred's lockdown was
so different from...

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.136
-I know, right?
-...anyone else's that I've --

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.906
-I feel like one of the things
a lot of people did in lockdowns

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:15.341
was forget people's birthdays.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:16.876
-And it seemed like Fred
really managed --

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.711
-But he was also going into
crowded places.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.380
Like, the doctor's office
had tons of patients.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.948
-Can you imagine going to
a doctor's office

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.883
twice in 10 days?
-He's like going for --

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.985
He's going to the sub shop.
There's tons of people there.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.053
-Yeah, you were doing
a lot of being out there.

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:30.422
-I was busy.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:31.691
-So, this is --

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.326
I'm actually fascinated.
I want to ask you something.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:36.228
Because we've had guests on
this week who I had interviewed

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:40.733
during the pandemic via Zoom,
but you actually were here

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.068
in January in this studio
without an audience.

00:01:43.068 --> 00:01:44.537
-Yes.
-How -- Do you remember

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.472
what that was like for you?
Did you think it was weird

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:47.740
being in this big studio
with nobody here?

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.442
-I really have no memory of it.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.211
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.646
You're kind of a reverse Fred
in that way.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.448
-I guess.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.316
Really, I have no memory of it
at all.

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:58.651
-I can tell you this.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.053
Hopefully you have some memory
of being here.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.787
You have been on the show now
11 times.

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:04.056
-11 times.
-That's really --

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:05.558
The other thing,
because I remember --

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.627
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. 11 times. That's great.

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:12.965
This show and "The Blacklist"
started the same year.

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:14.167
You were actually out here.
-And boy, have things

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.535
gone downhill.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:18.271
-Right? We don't even have
labels on the water anymore.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.906
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.974
Can you believe you've been
doing the show

00:02:21.974 --> 00:02:24.076
as long as you have?

00:02:24.076 --> 00:02:26.512
-It is a long time.
Ninth season.

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:30.082
-Yeah. I noticed from the clip
you had a shaved head.

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:31.251
-I did.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.685
-Is that a bald cap
or did you actually --

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.020
-No, no, no,
it was a shaved head.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.054
-So you did it?
-Yeah.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.789
-Alright.
-I mean, it isn't that much

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.425
further than this.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.859
-Yeah, how long did it take
to grow back?

00:02:40.859 --> 00:02:44.297
-It's just a couple more passes
really, you know?

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:51.003
Yes, this year starts -- this
season starts two years later,

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:56.309
and he was, you know, sort of
lost for a couple of years

00:02:56.309 --> 00:03:01.481
and came down with
terrible mange and so...

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.548
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:05.418
Terrible hot spots.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.486
And they had to get rid of it.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:08.253
-So he just had to get rid
of all it.

00:03:08.253 --> 00:03:10.823
Yuck, and start over.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.193
-You've always talked
on this show admiringly

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.295
about the writers on
"The Blacklist"

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:18.564
and how they continue to be
inventive and not just keep it

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.232
fresh for the audience
but for you.

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:21.701
Does that continue to be true?

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.035
Are you still excited to see
where they're going to take it?

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:26.105
-Yes. No, it's completely
self-serving in that --

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.207
You know, but, in all
seriousness, I mean,

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:34.746
that really was what I think
you have to look for in material

00:03:34.746 --> 00:03:36.716
that you're going to be doing
for a television show,

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.018
especially if it seems like
something that you want to

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.552
stick with for a little bit.

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:44.790
And I read the pilot of this,
and it was clear that

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.661
there was so -- you know,
the landscape was pretty broad

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:52.498
and the tone was very...

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:56.068
you know, at turns was
very irreverent and funny

00:03:56.068 --> 00:03:59.806
and at other times
incredibly intense.

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.177
And I realized that
this character really

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:08.847
could go anywhere and you could
take so many twists and turns

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:12.018
and surprises,
and it still continues to.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:14.654
-This is not your first foray
into television.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.489
You were on "The Office,"
we mentioned.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:17.724
You were also on "Boston Legal,"

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:19.559
where one of your costars,
Bill Shatner...

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.460
-Went to space.
-...went to outer space.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.195
Of your costars in your career,

00:04:23.195 --> 00:04:24.997
would he have been
your first choice to send?

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:27.099
-I think he'd be one of --

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:29.902
I think he might be one of --

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:33.472
I think was the best-suited.
-Yeah.

00:04:33.472 --> 00:04:35.674
[ Laughter ]
-Really, I mean, he really was,

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:37.676
besides that great suit
he was wearing.

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:38.578
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.246
He did let you -- Right.
It was --

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.915
I think for most men his age...
-Yes.

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:45.318
-...if you put them in
that suit, it would be jarring.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.919
And yet with him, it looked like

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:48.854
that's what he should
always be wearing.

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:51.490
-Yeah, no, I hope he kept it.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:54.427
And if he did, I'm sure it'll
show up on his website.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:58.698
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:01.034
-We'll be right back with more
from James spader.

